# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Derived / extracted data — do NOT commit.
#
# Per AGENT.md: "Keep original downloaded bytes separate from derived text,
# extracted archives, and summaries." The decompressed/unzipped derivatives are
# reproducible from the tracked publisher archives (.gz / .zip) via
# `scripts/backup_sources.py` + local decompression, so they are excluded here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Decompressed / unzipped derivative trees (explicitly named "extracted")
collusion-wiki/data/extracted/
swarmtraces/data/extracted/

# Catch any other "extracted" directory that may be created by future sources
**/data/extracted/

# ── Optional: widen to exclude ALL unzipped/uncompressed derivatives ──────────
# Uncomment the line below to also drop Transluce's publisher ZIP expansion
# (documented as the "extracted catalog"). Default: KEEP it tracked, since it is
# the publisher's intended layout and is described in transluce/data/README.md.
# transluce/data/catalog/

# ── Optional: narrow-scope safety net -------------------------------------------------
# Decompressed JSON/JSONL that has a compressed sibling (.gz). Add these only if
# you later hoist extracted files out of data/extracted/ into a source's data/.
# **/data/*.jsonl
# !**/data/*.jsonl.gz

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Original downloaded bytes and documentation are intentionally KEPT tracked:
#   - *.jsonl.gz / *.json.gz / *.zip            (publisher archives)
#   - *.pdf, article/, references/, data/*.csv, data/*.json
#   - README.md, AGENT.md, backup-manifest.json, inventory.json,
#     SHA256SUMS, verification.json
#   - scripts/, results/ (analysis docs)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OS / editor noise (not part of the archive)
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*~
*.swp
*.swo

# Python bytecode caches from running the local scripts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Transient downloader/lock artifacts (if any are ever written here)
*.download.lock
.download.lock
